8888	{"artifactId":"LLD-7d42920dbef28b51-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-7d42920dbef28b51-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-11T17:23:28.574Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"fix-targets-defect.1","ref":"fix-targets-defect","item":"fix-targets-defect","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The ISSUE's root cause is that planMigration resolves one label/anchor per work item but applies it only to the md destination path, never writing it back to meta; the fix intent asks for stored label and anchor to match the folder, with dry-run purity, all-or-nothing rollback, and metadata-only changes. The LLD's metaRewrites (epicSlug, epicCreatedAt, standalone) planned in planMigration and applied in applyMigration's per-group commit address this.","evidence":"ISSUE-7d42920dbef28b51.json rootCause: 'that label and anchor are applied only to the destination path, never written back to a member's meta'; fixIntent: 'keep the migration's dry-run purity and its all-or-nothing rollback, and be safe for already-approved artifacts (metadata alignment only, no body change)'. migrate-docs-tree.ts:424-448 computes `label`/`anchor`/`workItemKind` per group and uses them only in resolveArtifactMdPath. deriveMdPath (pending.ts:189-193) reads exactly epicSlug, epicCreatedAt ?? createdAt and standalone, so the three fields the LLD rewrites are the complete set path derivation depends on. [files: .insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-7d42920dbef28b51.json, src/workflow/migrate-docs-tree.ts, src/workflow/pending.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Today planMigration forces in-memory standalone true for SPEC, the folder key uses only the date+hash8 (not the full timestamp), and deriveMdPath reads the raw meta.standalone, so a raw-meta comparison and an epicSegment comparison are the right ones.","evidence":"migrate-docs-tree.ts:345 `standalone: meta.standalone === true || parsed.kind === 'SPEC'`; id.ts:213 `epicSegment: `E${wfid.date}${wfid.hash8}``; pending.ts:192 `meta['standalone'] === true ? 'standalone' : 'epic'`, pending.ts:190 `str(meta['epicCreatedAt']) ?? str(meta['createdAt'])`, pending.ts:193 `str(meta['epicSlug']) ?? hash` (so a hash-fallback group with no stored slug already derives the hash label, which justifies skipping epicSlug rewrites there). [files: src/workflow/migrate-docs-tree.ts, src/workflow/id.ts, src/workflow/pending.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"applyMigration currently returns early on zero moves, before the clean-tree check (so the early-return change is needed for rewrite-only plans, and the clean-tree refusal then precedes any rewrite).","evidence":"migrate-docs-tree.ts:662-665 `if (plan.moves.length === 0) { log.info(...nothing to migrate...); return; }` precedes the porcelain check at :668-670 and the pinned startSha at :673; rollback at :714 `reset --hard startSha; clean -fd docs`. The LLD's postcondition 'Runs when moves OR metaRewrites is non-empty' covers this, and with it the clean-tree check runs before any rewrite as the error-paths section says. [files: src/workflow/migrate-docs-tree.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The md label lines to edit are where the LLD says (plan.ts:121, lld.ts:336, extend.ts:59/61, define.ts epicShortName, hld.ts hldShortName), and those short-name helpers fall back to body text, so the planner must reuse (export) them.","evidence":"plan.ts:121 and lld.ts:336 `**Epic:** \\`${meta.epicSlug}\\``; extend.ts:59 `# Extend: ${meta.epicSlug} — ${body.addedStory.title}` and :61 `> **Extends Epic \\`${meta.epicSlug}\\`**`; define.ts:163-167 epicShortName returns slug else firstSentence(body.problem); hld.ts:236-240 hldShortName returns slug else firstLine(body.frameworkSummary). Both are currently non-exported `function`s, matching the LLD's step 1 'export epicShortName / hldShortName'. Note: readMeta (migrate-docs-tree.ts:276-285) parses only meta, so the planner must also read the DEF/HLD body to compute the old short name; the LLD's 'reuse those helpers' implies that, but it is an extra read the implementer must add. [files: src/workflow/artifacts/plan.ts, src/workflow/artifacts/lld.ts, src/workflow/artifacts/extend.ts, src/workflow/artifacts/define.ts, src/workflow/artifacts/hld.ts, src/workflow/migrate-docs-tree.ts]","action":"When implementing, pass the full parsed DEF/HLD artifact (not readMeta's subset) to the exported short-name helpers.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The only consumer of MigrationPlan is src/bin/insrc-migrate-docs.ts, which prints moves/links/unmappable in the dry run and must be extended to print metaRewrites (and its 'Applied' line).","evidence":"insrc-migrate-docs.ts:25-42 calls planMigration, prints `move`/`link`/`UNMAPPABLE` lines, then applyMigration. No other caller was found in src outside tests. The LLD lists this file as a call site for both MetaRewrite and MigrationPlan. [files: src/bin/insrc-migrate-docs.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.1","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Re-writing a patched JSON with 2-space indent and a trailing newline matches the artifact store's own formatting, so only the patched meta fields differ and an untouched member stays byte-identical.","evidence":"Store writers serialize as `JSON.stringify(x, null, 2) + '\\n'` (gates.ts:202, questions.ts:418, tracker/refs.ts:96, bugfix/stamp.ts:87). JSON.parse/stringify preserves key insertion order, so a patch that only sets existing or new meta keys leaves body/citations/approvedAt untouched. Consistent members get no MetaRewrite, so they are never rewritten. [files: src/workflow/gates.ts, src/workflow/questions.ts, src/workflow/bugfix/stamp.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.2","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The per-group commit and the reset --hard rollback can cover the rewrites: commits are path-scoped per group and the rollback resets to the pinned start SHA.","evidence":"migrate-docs-tree.ts:706-709 commits each group with `'--', ...paths` built only from move from/to paths, so the rewritten JSON and edited md paths must be added to that pathspec (the LLD's step 2 says this: 'include their files in each group's chunk commit'), and rewrite-only groups need their own commit since byGroup is built from moves alone (:701-705). Rollback at :714 resets to startSha, which undoes JSON edits under .insrc as well (the `clean -fd docs` only matters for untracked files, and the rewritten JSONs are tracked). [files: src/workflow/migrate-docs-tree.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each acceptance criterion (ac1 folder agreement, ac2 dry-run purity, ac3 rollback, ac4 metadata-only) maps to a test that fails on today's code.","evidence":"ac1: 'after apply, deriveMdPath on every member's stored meta equals where its md sits' fails today, because the JSON is never written (the defect the ISSUE reproduces). ac2: the CLI test expecting one line per metadata rewrite fails today, because insrc-migrate-docs.ts:28-31 prints no such lines. ac3: the two-group test asserts the rewrite-step error message after a committed md/JSON change, and no rewrite step exists today. ac4: 'only the planned meta fields change' requires a rewrite to exist, which is absent today, and the existing byte-identical test is explicitly inverted (migration step 4). The purity half of ac2 (metaRewrites: [] and byte-identical after planning) would pass without the fix, but the same criterion also has the CLI test, which would fail. [files: src/workflow/__tests__/migrate-docs-tree.test.ts, src/bin/insrc-migrate-docs.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":8,"unverified":0},"template":"design-issue","reviewedAt":"2026-10-11T17:23:28.574Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
